{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules-table2-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules-table2-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 2 from rem:ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules-table2-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules-table2-data\"></a><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code></th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathtt{ckFromReduction}\\ q\\ k</code></th>\n<th>source of closed form</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">0</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n<td>baseline</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">1</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b</code></td>\n<td>Kashiwara <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde f_1</code> matrix element on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_{(2,1)}</code> (Rules 1+2+3)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">2</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b^2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde f_1^\\dagger \\tilde f_1</code> return amplitude (Rules 1+2+3)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">3</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-2 = J_{\\mathrm{Hopf}}(q=1)</code></td>\n<td>3-fold Markov closure <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\to</code> Hopf substructure <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\to</code> KL classical limit (Rules 1+4)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">4</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_3 \\cdot b^4 = -2 b^4</code></td>\n<td>Jones <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\times</code> Kashiwara multiplicative mixing — Rules 1+3+4 (the old <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b^2 + 1/2</code> value belongs at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k = 5</code> with a sign flip; superseded)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">5</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-(b^2 + 1/2)</code></td>\n<td>Kashiwara <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b^2</code> + Hopf-half offset (mixed intra/inter) — the form originally attributed to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k = 4</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\geq 5</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n<td>open R&#x26;D (see <a href=\"#prop:categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms\"><code>prop:categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms</code></a>)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/ck-extraction-from-algebraic-rules-table2-data.md","heading":"Table"}
